# Granot Form Leads Workflow

- `src/parsers/granot/form-leads.ts` parses Booked Jobs / Follow Up Estimates rows and validates `prior` independently from identity. Provider refs, Mongo ids, and blank refs are all candidates for server-side resolution. Only `prior` values `1` and `5` are field-syncable; `0` remains eligible for receiver-only enrichment after identity resolves.
- `src/parsers/granot/form-edit-lead.ts` parses the current edit page (`ORDREF` + priority level) and also exposes `applyBindingEstimateFeeFromInitialPrice()`, which writes `Binding Estimate Fee` at 85% of the initial price into the first extra-fee fields.
- `scan.ts` sends `PARSE_FOLLOW_UP_ROWS` and returns the parsed response plus the row ids selected by default.
- `preview.ts` calls the authoritative `POST /api/v1/form-leads/granot-match` interface with ref, phone, email, name, source label, and prior. The server owns the exact-ref → Mongo-id → source-gated fallback ladder and returns `ref_no_exact`, `mongo_id`, `fallback`, or `none`.
- `payloads.ts` owns sync predicates and payload shaping. No row is syncable until preview returns one resolved Vantage `_id`; conflicted and cross-source rows stay blocked. Apply uses the dedicated drift-checked Granot PATCH endpoint with the preview/source snapshot; the server atomically enforces non-duplicate, fill-only location, and empty-receiver preconditions. For `prior` `1`/`5`, it parses Granot locations into fill-only Vantage fields.
- **Location backfill (form leads only, conservative).** `buildFormLeadUpdatePayload()` fills location fields only when Vantage is missing data — it never overwrites valid values. Cities write when `pickup_city` / `delivery_city` is blank. States write only when `pickup_state` / `delivery_state` is missing, including the `FORM_LEAD_UNKNOWN_STATE` sentinel (`"not_found"`) that `FormLead` defaults to when zip lookup fails at creation. ZIPs write when `pickup_zip` / `destination_zip` is blank or all zeros, but only if the existing state is also missing or already matches the Granot state. State writes require the same ZIP alignment (missing ZIP or ZIP matches Granot) so the extension does not combine a Granot state with a conflicting existing ZIP. Prior `0` rows never carry location candidates.
- `preview-model.ts` reuses `buildFormLeadUpdatePayload()` so preview state remains accurate, but owner-facing `changes[]` suppresses city/ZIP details. It only names a location update when `pickup_state` or `delivery_state` currently equals `"not_found"` and Granot supplies the replacement state.
- `sync.ts` compares the candidate against the current Vantage lead, PATCHes only changed fields, and still sends an idempotent payload when nothing changed so the server can perform its own sync path. During sync it also attempts **receiver-agent attribution** from `salesRepRaw`: `buildReceiverAgentUpdate()` normalizes the value and calls `matchAgentByCrmUsername()` in `src/workflows/agents/match.ts` against the loaded Agent catalog's `granot_crm_username`. When exactly one Agent matches and the Form Lead has no `receiver_agent` yet, the PATCH adds `receiver_agent`, `receiver_agent_source: "extension_crm_username_match"`, and `receiver_agent_source_value`. Existing `receiver_agent` values are never overwritten; unmatched or already-linked cases only append informational text to the row result message.
- `src/workflows/agents/loadForReceiverMatching.ts` loads the Agent catalog (`includeInactive: true`) for sync and background auto-sync. Popup sync uses `resolveAgentsForReceiverMatching()` with the ephemeral `app.state.agents` cache; the background runner calls `loadAgentsForReceiverMatching()` directly.
- `src/entrypoints/popup/ui/salesRep.ts` renders the owner-only **Sales Rep** control on each form-leads row after preview resolves a Vantage `_id`. CRM-username match (`extension_crm_username_match`) is preferred over first-name match (`extension_match`); zero matches open a create-or-pick dialog. Manual links use the same `receiver_agent` provenance fields as auto-sync and are the only path that can overwrite an existing link (via explicit owner action).
- `cycles.ts` turns parsed rows and row results into the UI-free `CycleDetail` format shared with auto-sync history.
- The tests in `src/test/form-leads-payloads.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-preview-model.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-preview.test.ts`, `src/test/form-leads-sync.test.ts`, and `src/test/parsers.test.ts` document the intended identity, duplicate, location backfill, and sync behavior.

